{
  "abstract": "A two-dimensional family of quaternionic Pryms contains an eightfold whose two orthogonal multiplicity systems are correlated with two genus-four Jacobians. The algebraicity of the resulting mixed tensor does not follow from the Hodge conjecture for powers of the three individual factors. We construct that tensor using two explicit dihedral correspondences between surfaces. The first correspondence, established previously, leads from a quotient of a genus-29 curve squared to a surface with an elliptic Albanese pencil. A second degree-two function on the elliptic base gives a new bigonal tower with rational norm. Its partner is birational to the diagonal quaternion quotient of the two genus-four curves. We verify the entire double-cover multiplier and the descent involution, including its hyperelliptic sign. The composite correspondence has transpose-composition four on the rank-sixteen moving cohomology. A full stabilizer calculation then proves the rational Hodge conjecture on every power of the correlated product of the two fourfolds and the eightfold. The same augmentation supplies all degree-one representations needed for generalized Hodge support, giving the generalized Hodge conjecture on its powers. After spreading the correspondence, both conclusions hold on a fixed nonempty smooth parameter open whenever at least one source Jacobian is non-CM, including the non-CM isogeny loci. The one-CM case uses a maximal-torus calculation with connected inverse image. No assertion is made for pairs with two CM sources or arbitrary quaternionic eightfolds.",
